# __name__

A minimal Go CLI generated by [weld](../../README.md). The project is pure Go
today: no web dependency, no empty placeholder directories.

## Commands

```sh
go run . serve --addr :8080   # start the HTTP server
go run . version              # print the version
go run . help                 # show help

make build                    # build bin/__name__
make run                      # run the server
make test                     # run the Go tests
```

`serve` exposes `GET /api/health` returning `{"status":"ok"}`.

## Capabilities

The project is scaffolded from the `base` capability (v__version__). Every file
weld wrote is recorded in `weld.json`, together with the capability and version
that produced it.

Capabilities are additive. To add the React + TypeScript + Vite frontend:

```sh
weld add web
```

That command adds `web/`, embeds its build output through the
`internal/server` asset extension point, and wires `make build` to build the
frontend. Use `weld list` to see what is available and installed.

The `weld add api` capability (HTTP contract, go-validate rules, OpenAPI) is
roadmap and deliberately not faked here.

## Layout

```
main.go                      command entry point
internal/app/                command dispatch and serve wiring
internal/server/             HTTP handler and the asset extension point
Makefile                     build/run/test entry points
weld.json                    manifest of capability-managed files
```
